\section*{1. Heat Fin}
The governing equation is
\begin{equation}\frac{d^2T}{dx^2}=MT,\qquad 0\le x\le1.\end{equation}
All numerical solutions below use $N=1001$ grid points and centered second-order finite differences. No full matrix is constructed.

\subsection*{1.1 Finite-Difference Equations and Tridiagonal Storage}
At an interior node $x_i=i\Delta x$,
\[
\frac{T_{i-1}-2T_i+T_{i+1}}{\Delta x^2}=M_iT_i,
\]
so
\[
T_{i-1}-(2+M_i\Delta x^2)T_i+T_{i+1}=0.
\]
Thus the three diagonals requested in the problem are
\[
\boxed{d_i=-(2+M_i\Delta x^2),\qquad a_i=1,\qquad b_i=1.}
\]
Here $d,a,b$ denote the main, lower, and upper diagonals. The known value $T_0=1$ is moved to the right-hand side of the first interior equation. For $T(1)=0$, the last prescribed value is handled the same way. For $T'(1)=0$, a centered ghost-point condition gives $T_N=T_{N-2}$; substitution into the differential equation at the tip gives
\[
2T_{N-2}-(2+M_{N-1}\Delta x^2)T_{N-1}=\Delta x^2f_{N-1}.
\]
This retains tridiagonal form. The Thomas algorithm performs forward elimination and backward substitution in $O(N)$ work and $O(N)$ storage.

For constant $M$, the discrete homogeneous recurrence has $T_i=C_+r_+^i+C_-r_-^i$, where
\[
r_{\pm}=\frac{2+M\Delta x^2\pm\sqrt{(2+M\Delta x^2)^2-4}}{2}.
\]

\subsection*{1.2 Closed-Form Continuous Solutions}
Let $k=\sqrt M$. The general solution is $T=A\cosh(kx)+B\sinh(kx)$.
For $T(0)=1,T(1)=0$,
\begin{equation}\boxed{T(x)=\frac{\sinh(k(1-x))}{\sinh k}}.\end{equation}
For $T(0)=1,T'(1)=0$,
\begin{equation}\boxed{T(x)=\frac{\cosh(k(1-x))}{\cosh k}}.\end{equation}

\subsection*{1.3 Part (b): Prescribed Temperatures}
The cold-reservoir heat flux is $q(1)=-T'(1)$ and is evaluated numerically with the second-order backward difference
\[
-T'(1)\approx-\frac{3T_{N-1}-4T_{N-2}+T_{N-3}}{2\Delta x}.
\]
